==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|rēch}}, {{IPA|en|/ɹiːt͡ʃ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-reach.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːtʃ|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|reech}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*Hreyǵ-|id=stretch}}
From {{inh|en|enm|rechen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rǣċan|t=to reach}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*raikijan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*raikijaną}}, from the {{der|en|ine-pro|*Hreyǵ-|t=to bind, reach|id=stretch}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nl|reiken}}, {{cog|de|reichen}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|+|+|+,raught<l:obsolete>}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[extend]], [[stretch]], or [[thrust]] out (for example a limb or object held in the hand).
#: {{ux|en|He '''reached''' for a weapon that was on the table.}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''reached''' for his shoe with his legs.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}}  To give to someone by stretching out a [[limb]], especially the hand; to give with the hand; to pass to another person; to [[hand over]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''reach''' someone a book}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To stretch out the hand.
# {{lb|en|intransitive|colloquial}} To raise one's hands above one's head as a sign of surrender.
#: {{ux|en|"You'd better '''reach''', sheriff!" warned the cowboy.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To attain or obtain by [[stretch]]ing forth the hand; to extend some part of the body, or something held, so as to touch, [[strike]], [[grasp]], etc.
#: {{ux|en|to '''reach''' an object with the hand, or with a spear}}
#: {{ux|en|“I can't quite '''reach''' the pepper. Could you pass it to me?”}}
#: {{ux|en|The gun was stored in a small box on a high closet shelf, but the boy managed to '''reach''' it by climbing on other boxes.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|of a [[missile]]}} To strike or touch.
#: {{ux|en|His bullet '''reached''' its intended target.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|by extension}} To extend an [[action]], effort, or [[influence]] to; to [[penetrate]] to; to pierce, or cut.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1889|journal=The Kindergarten-Primary Magazine|volume=1|page=119
|passage=A few words, lovingly, encouragingly spoken failed to '''reach''' her heart.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=4|passage=Judge Short had gone to town, and Farrar was off for a three days' cruise up the lake. I was bitterly regretting I had not gone with him when the distant notes of a coach horn '''reached''' my ear, and I descried a four-in-hand winding its way up the inn road from the direction of Mohair.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To extend to; to stretch out as far as; to touch [[by virtue of]] extent.
#: {{ux|en|his hand '''reaches''' the river}}
#: {{ux|en|When the forest '''reaches''' the river, you will be able to rest.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=III|passage=Thy desire {{...}} leads to no excess / That '''reaches''' blame.|year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[arrive]] at (a place) by effort of any kind.
#: {{ux|en|After three years, he '''reached''' the position of manager.}}
#: {{ux|en|The climbers '''reached''' the top of the mountain after a gruelling ten-day hike.}}
#* {{RQ:Cheyne Philosophical Principles|edition=2nd|part=I|title=Part I Preface 2|page=15|passage=I am very Senſible, the beſt accounts of the Appearances of Nature (in any ſingle Inſtance hovv minute or ſimple ſoever) Humane Penetration can '''reach''', comes infinitely ſhort of its reality, and internal Conſtitution; for ''vvho can ſearch out the Almighty, or his vvorks to Perfection''.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=5|passage=But Miss Thorn relieved the situation by laughing aloud,{{nb...}}. By the time we '''reached''' the house we were thanking our stars she had come. Mrs. Cooke came out from under the port-cochere to welcome her.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|year=1956
|month=October
|author=Grace Liu
|title=A Train Trip in China
|journal=New World Review
|url=https://archive.org/details/sim_update-ussr_1956-10_24_10/
|location=New York
|publisher=S.R.T. Publications
|volume=24
|issue=10
|issn=0028-7067
|oclc=8299959
|page=20
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_update-ussr_1956-10_24_10/page/20/
|column=1
|text=On the trip out our car was full of railway workers, going out to work on the Lanchow-Sinkiang Railway which had already '''reached''' Yumen, China’s biggest oil field, and in 1960 will connect with the Soviet Union’s Turkestan-Siberia Railway; or to the Lanchow-Yinchuan section, which cuts through the Great Wall to '''reach''' Yinchuan, a major wool, hide and skin trading center in the Northwest.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} To make [[contact]] with.
#: {{syn|en|contact|get hold of|get in touch}}
#: {{usex|en|I tried to '''reach''' you all day.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} To [[connect]] with (someone) on an [[emotional]] level, making them [[receptive]] of (one); to [[get through]] to (someone).
#: {{ux|en|What will it take for me to '''reach''' him?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1949|author={{w|Friedrich Hayek|F. A. Hayek}}|title=The Intellectuals and Socialism|journal={{w|University of Chicago Law Review}}|publisher={{w|University of Chicago}}|location={{w|Chicago}}|volume=16|number=3|doi=10.2307/1597903|page=418|passage=Whether by design or driven by the force of circumstances, they have always directed their main effort toward gaining the support of this "elite," while the more conservative groups have acted, as regularly but unsuccessfully, on a more naive view of mass democracy and have usually vainly tried directly to '''reach''' and to persuade the individual voter.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|India|Singapore}} To arrive at a particular destination.
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=Mr. Free Notes|title=Getting bus from KL to Singapore leaving night, likely to be any delays in arrival?
|newsgroup=soc.culture.singapore |url=https://groups.google.com/forum/#!search/%22reaching$20at%22$20singapore%7Csort:relevance/soc.culture.singapore/iDXn3VdTgRI/TT8pIG7oeykJ
|date=18 February 2004 |passage=I suggest taking an earlier bus (say 6:00 p.m.), '''reaching''' at around midnight, then taking a taxi (might even be able to catch the last MRT) to Changi.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=Rakesh Chandrasekar|title=Post Trek Mail II - Freshers Trek April 22nd Nagala West
|newsgroup=The Chennai Trekking Club |url=https://groups.google.com/forum/#!search/%22once$20we$20reached$2C$20we%22/sachennaitrekkingclub/8lZP9k80zkE/vEtbyK8tXGwJ
|date=26 April 2012 |passage=Once we '''reached''', we parked our cars beneath the trees and started trekking up the hill after a brief round of introductions.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To continue living until or up to (a certain age).
#: {{usex|en|You can only access the inheritance money when you '''reach''' the age of 25.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To understand; to comprehend.
#* {{RQ:Beaumont Fletcher Comedies and Tragedies|A King and No King|4|2|passage=Do what, sir? I '''reach''' you not.}}
# To [[strain]] after something; to make (sometimes futile or pretentious) efforts.
#: {{ux|en|'''Reach''' for your dreams.}}
#: {{usex|en|'''Reach''' for the stars!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=Janet S. Steinwedel|title=The Golden Key to Executive Coaching
|passage=Repetitious comments are other examples of introjects that we take on as if they were truths. These include: You're lazy; you're selfish; you'll never amount to anything; you have big dreams; don't you think you're '''reaching''' a bit; try something more attainable; you were never good in math; you're not quick on your feet; you're oblivious to the world around you.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To extend in [[dimension]], time etc.; to [[stretch]] out [[continuously]] ({{m|en|past}}, {{m|en|beyond}}, {{m|en|above}}, {{m|en|from}} etc. something).
#* {{RQ:Mandela Long Walk to Freedom|year=2010|page=4|passage=The Thembu tribe '''reaches''' back for twenty generations to {{w|Zwide kaLanga|King Zwide}}.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} To sail on the wind, as from one point of tacking to another, or with the wind nearly [[abeam]].
# {{lb|en|slang|MTE|MLE}} To arrive at a particular [[destination]], especially to [[join]] someone; to [[meet up]].
#: {{syn|en|link up}}
#: {{ux|en|What time you '''reaching''' tomorrow?}}

[[File:Barge Match (Thames River) RMG PY4069.tiff|thumb|Thames barges reaching on the Thames; they are probably on ''Gravesend Reach'']]

=====Usage notes=====
* In the past, {{m|en|raught}}, {{m|en|rought}} and {{m|en|retcht}} could be found as past tense forms; these are now obsolete, except perhaps in some dialects.

