====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

[[File:River Thames Reaches.jpg|thumb|An old map of the reaches of the River Thames; it can be seen that a reach is a straightish stretch (and can therefore be sailed in one reach, one straight-line path between [[:wikipedia:Tacking (sailing)|tacks]], unless the wind is too close to head-on to allow the sailing-boat to [[:wikipedia:Point of sail#Reaching|reach]])]]

# The act of stretching or extending; [[extension]].<ref name=Webster>{{R:Webster 1913}}</ref>
# The ability to reach or touch with the person, a limb, or something held or thrown.
#: {{ux|en|The fruit is beyond my '''reach'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|to be within '''reach''' of cannon shot}}
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Land That Time Forgot||VI|passage={{...}} and we have learned not to fire at any of the dinosaurs unless we can keep out of their '''reach''' for at least two minutes after hitting them in the brain or spine, or five minutes after puncturing their hearts&mdash;it takes them so long to die.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=A Further Range|author={{w|Robert Frost}}|chapter=The Vindictives|year=1936|passage=You like to hear about gold.<br>A king filled his prison room<br>As full as the room could hold<br>To the top of his '''reach''' on the wall<br>With every known shape of the stuff.}}
# The power of stretching out or extending action, influence, or the like; power of [[attainment]] or [[management]]; extent of force or capacity.
#* {{RQ:Hayward Edward 6|passage=Drawn by others who had deeper '''reaches''' than themselves to matters which they least intended.}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Essay on Criticism|passage=Be sure yourself and your own '''reach''' to know.}}
# Extent; stretch; expanse; hence, [[application]]; influence; result; scope.
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|text=And on the left hand, hell, / With long '''reach''', interposed.|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Othello|III|iii|passage=I am to pray you not to strain my speech / To grosser issues, nor to larger '''reach''' / Than to suspicion.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=Evan J. Mandery|title=The Campaign: Rudy Giuliani, Ruth Messenger, Al Sharpton, and the Race to be Mayor of New York City
|passage=While points measure the number of times the average person in a group sees an ad, '''reach''' measures the percentage of people in a group that see an ad at least once. Increasing the '''reach''' of an ad becomes increasingly expensive as you go along (for the mathematically inclined, it is an exponential function).}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} An [[exaggeration]]; an extension beyond evidence or normal; a [[stretch]].
#: {{ux|en|To call George eloquent is certainly a '''reach'''.}}
# {{lb|en|boxing}} The distance a boxer's arm can extend to land a blow.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} Any [[point of sail]] in which the wind comes from the side of a vessel, excluding [[close-hauled]].
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[distance]] [[traverse]]d between [[tack]]s.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A stretch of a watercourse which can be sailed in one reach (in the previous sense). An extended [[portion]] of water; a stretch; a straightish portion of a stream, river, or arm of the sea extending up into the land, as from one turn to another. By extension, the adjacent land.
#* {{RQ:Pliny Holland Historie of the World
|passage=the gulfe Iasius, and all the coast thereof is very full of creekes and '''reaches'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam
|passage=The river's wooded '''reach'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Conrad Heart of Darkness|page=483|passage=The '''reaches''' opened before us and closed behind, as if the forest had stepped leisurely across the water to bar the way for our return.}}
# A level stretch of a watercourse, as between rapids in a river or locks in a [[canal]]. (examples?)
# An extended [[portion]] or area of land or water.
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Age of Consent|year=1962|page=134|passage=Lower down, in a little '''reach''' of the lagoon there grew a clump of casuarinas, those timid isolates that withdraw from other trees, selecting their own privacy, which is for ever whispering secrets up in their feathery fronds, set in motion by the slightest breeze.}}
#*: {{quote|en|Through eerie '''reach''' of ancient woods / Where lumbering mists arise / I journey for nines moons of the year / To where a land of legend lies}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} An article to obtain an [[advantage]].
#* {{RQ:Bacon War with Spain|passage=The Duke of Parma had particular '''reaches''' and ends of his own, under hand, to cross the design.}}
# The [[pole]] or [[rod]] connecting the [[rear]] [[axle]] with the forward [[bolster]] of a [[wagon]].<ref name=Webster />
#* {{quote-book|en|1913|{{w|Alice B. Emerson}}|[[s:Ruth Fielding at Snow Camp|Ruth Fielding at Snow Camp]]|section=[[s:Ruth Fielding at Snow Camp/Chapter 7|Chapter 7]]|text=They leaped ahead just as Ruth came to the side of the long '''reach''' that connected the small pair of front wheels with the huge wheels in the rear.}}

